# MintRadar Backend — Environment Variables
# Copy to .env and fill in real values. Never commit .env.

# PostgreSQL connection string (used by pg Pool in db.ts)
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/mintradar

# Port the Express server listens on (default: 3002)
PORT=3002

# Node environment — set to "production" in prod to suppress debug logs
# and restrict CORS to the live origin only
NODE_ENV=production

# Comma-separated list of allowed CORS origins
# (new primary domain first, old domain kept as a fallback while both run in parallel)
# Dev default: https://mintradar.org,https://mintradar.pedani.eu,http://localhost:5173
# Prod default: https://mintradar.org,https://mintradar.pedani.eu
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://mintradar.org,https://mintradar.pedani.eu

# Optional. nsec of the "MintRadar Alerts" service identity used to send
# Nostr DM notifications (mint down/up transitions) to subscribers. Held in
# memory only for the process lifetime, never written to any storage. If
# unset, notification sending is disabled and the rest of the backend
# (probing, existing endpoints) is unaffected.
# NOTIFICATION_SERVICE_NSEC=nsec1...

# Optional. nsec of the "MintRadar Health" identity that signs the Nostr health assertions (kind 30385). Its public
# key must equal ATTESTATION_PUBKEY_HEX in src/healthAssertions.ts, otherwise the feature stays off. Unset or empty:
# the feature is dormant (one log line, no timers, no network, no database writes). Never log or commit it; it is
# separate from NOTIFICATION_SERVICE_NSEC. See docs/claude/nostr-health-assertions.md.
# ATTESTATION_SERVICE_NSEC=…

# Optional. Private mode: comma-separated list of mint URLs (https:// only), e.g.
# MINT_ALLOWLIST=https://mint.example.com,https://other-mint.example.org
# Monitors only these mints: no discovery, no reviews sync, no health assertions (kind 30385), no cashu.info sync,
# submit/discover/probe answer 403 for other URLs. Empty or no valid https:// entry = normal mode. If NOTIFICATION_SERVICE_NSEC
# is set, DM notifications still carry the mint hostname and link through Nostr relays. See "Private mode" in README.md.
# MINT_ALLOWLIST=
